    "created_at": "2016-10-07T18:54:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-07T18:54:31Z",
    "body": "> use a unified watchAvailability(...) function that works like an event listener but 1) is guaranteed to be called at least once, and 2) can specify registration to have side-effects, which event listeners can't.\n\nThis sounds scary to me; it would be better to separate out the side effects into one method call, and continue using event listeners for the event.\n",
